Subject: [overlay 0002] Drop the Unix main() entry on iOS

src/unix/system.c defines int main() + the desktop while(!terminate) loop. On
iOS the OS owns the run loop (UIApplicationMain in the app), so guard the Unix
entry out on the whole iPhone-derived family — TARGET_OS_IPHONE covers iOS AND
visionOS/tvOS (where TARGET_OS_IOS is 0), all of which use UIApplicationMain
(kept on macOS/Linux). Pairs with the app's CADisplayLink driver (M2).

Apply from vendor root:  patch -p1 -d vendor/q2repro < this
diff --git a/src/unix/system.c b/src/unix/system.c
index fdbcf292..c212ab61 100644
--- a/src/unix/system.c
+++ b/src/unix/system.c
@@ -552,6 +552,10 @@ const sys_getinstalledgamepath_func_t gamepath_funcs[] = {
 };
 
 
+#if defined(__APPLE__)
+#include <TargetConditionals.h>
+#endif
+#if !(defined(__APPLE__) && TARGET_OS_IPHONE)
 /*
 =================
 main
@@ -595,3 +599,4 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 
     return EXIT_FAILURE; // never gets here
 }
+#endif // !(__APPLE__ && TARGET_OS_IPHONE) — iOS/visionOS provide their own UIApplicationMain entry
